    "created_at": "2016-08-23T18:41:51Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-08-23T18:41:51Z",
    "body": "Woah, I missed that. Hm... I think this spec is still the original definition of the document's origin, since HTML says \n\n> If the Document was obtained in some other manner … The default behaviour as defined in the WHATWG DOM standard applies. \n\nThat said, if you think HTML should provide the `<dfn for=document>`, that also makes sense to me. I'm just going for a consistent convention that when we write \"A foo's bar\", that we have a `<dfn for=foo>bar</dfn>`.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
